  "decision": {
    "answer": "SUPPORTS",
    "explanation": "The provided evidence from pmid-31871216 describes a case of squamous cell carcinoma (specifically involving the alveolar ridge and maxillary sinus, which is consistent with head and neck squamous cell carcinoma, a category that includes basaloid variants) with a somatic DPYD fusion deletion resulting in an in-frame deletion of exons 11-19. The patient was treated with a combination of Fluorouracil and Leucovorin and experienced a rapid and sustained clinical and radiographic response. This directly supports the claim that the DPYD EXON 11-19 DELETION is associated with sensitivity/response to the Fluorouracil and Leucovorin combination therapy in this context.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "document_id": "pmid-31871216",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 599,
        "quote": "Pathology evaluation of the resected ulcer (with a right hemimaxillectomy and right-sided neck dissection) identified a 3.5-cm well-differentiated squamous cell carcinoma involving the alveolar ridge and maxillary sinus with bone invasion; level I and II (but not III/IV) nodes were involved . . . Based on the findings of the POG analysis, treatment with weekly 5-FU (500 mg/m2) and leucovorin (20 mg/m2) was initiated. He had a rapid response (Fig. 1) both clinically and radiographically that was sustained for 17 wk. . . . A somatic fusion deletion event in the DPYD gene predicted to result in "
      },
      {
        "document_id": "pmid-31871216",
        "start": 599,
        "end": 689,
        "quote": "an in-frame deletion of exons 11-19 was detected in the genome and transcriptome (Fig. 2)."
      }
    ],
